        ":question/id": "3e8c0698-bfdd-52c7-9c90-69265bc9f4ed",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-69637",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $(L-M)-N$, where\n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,M=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,N=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(L-M)-N & =(\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -5\\end{bmatrix})-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0-1 & 5-(-1) & 5-0 \\\\ 4-(-2) & 3-3 & 1-(-5)\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1-(-1) & 6-4 & 5-3 \\\\ 6-5 & 0-5 & 6-0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      }
    ],
